1
00:04:06,428 --> 00:04:12,428
Courage is immortal.

2
00:08:12,857 --> 00:08:18,857
Thor is a adventure, fantasy, action film directed by Kenneth Branagh.

3
00:12:19,285 --> 00:12:25,285
Against his father Odin's will, The Mighty Thor - a powerful but
arrogant warrior god - recklessly reignites an ancient war.

4
00:16:25,714 --> 00:16:31,714
Thor is cast down to Earth and forced to live among humans as punishment.

5
00:20:32,142 --> 00:20:38,142
Once here, Thor learns what it takes to be a true hero when the most dangerous
villain of his world sends the darkest forces of Asgard to invade Earth.

6
00:24:38,571 --> 00:24:44,571
Thor, played by Chris Hemsworth.

7
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:51,000
Jane Foster, played by Natalie Portman.

8
00:32:51,428 --> 00:32:57,428
Loki, played by Tom Hiddleston.

9
00:36:57,857 --> 00:37:03,857
Odin, played by Anthony Hopkins.

10
00:41:04,285 --> 00:41:10,285
Erik Selvig, played by Stellan Skarsgård.

11
00:45:10,714 --> 00:45:16,714
Darcy Lewis, played by Kat Dennings.

12
00:49:17,142 --> 00:49:23,142
Thor is a 2011 American superhero film based on the
Marvel Comics character of the same name.

13
00:53:23,571 --> 00:53:29,571
Produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Paramount Pictures, it is
the fourth film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

14
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
It was directed by Kenneth Branagh, written by the writing team of Ashley Edward Miller and Zack Stentz along with Don Payne, and stars Chris Hemsworth as the title character alongside
Natalie Portman, Tom Hiddleston, Stellan Skarsgård, Kat Dennings, Clark Gregg, Colm Feore, Ray Stevenson, Idris Elba, Jaimie Alexander, Rene Russo, and Anthony Hopkins.

15
01:01:36,428 --> 01:01:42,428
After reigniting a dormant war, Thor is banished from Asgard to
Earth, stripped of his powers and his hammer Mjölnir.

16
01:05:42,857 --> 01:05:48,857
As his brother Loki (Hiddleston) plots to take the
Asgardian throne, Thor must prove himself worthy.

17
01:09:49,285 --> 01:09:55,285
Sam Raimi first developed the concept of a film adaptation based on Thor in 1991, but soon
abandoned the project, leaving it in "development hell" for several years.

18
01:13:55,714 --> 01:14:01,714
During this time, the rights were picked up by various film studios until Marvel signed Mark Protosevich
to develop the project in 2006, and planned to finance and release it through Paramount.

19
01:18:02,142 --> 01:18:08,142
Matthew Vaughn was assigned to direct the film for a tentative 2010 release.

20
01:22:08,571 --> 01:22:14,571
However, after Vaughn was released from his holding deal in 2008, Branagh was
approached and the film's release was rescheduled to 2011.

21
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:21,000
The main characters were cast in 2009, and principal photography took
place in California and New Mexico from January to May 2010.

22
01:30:21,428 --> 01:30:27,428
The film was converted to 3D in post-production.

23
01:34:27,857 --> 01:34:33,857
Thor premiered in Sydney on April 17, 2011, and was released in the
United States on May 6, as part of Phase One of the MCU.

24
01:38:34,285 --> 01:38:40,285
It received generally positive reviews from critics and was a
financial success, earning $449.3 million worldwide.

25
01:42:40,714 --> 01:42:46,714
Three sequels have been released: Thor: The Dark World (2013), Thor:
Ragnarok (2017), and Thor: Love and Thunder (2022).

26
01:46:47,142 --> 01:46:53,142
The film explores themes of new mexico, superhero,
redemption, banishment, based on comic.

27
01:50:53,571 --> 01:50:59,571
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
